WEBVTT

00:00:06.176 --> 00:00:09.512
I'm going out.
There's something I want to check on.

00:00:09.512 --> 00:00:11.548
Integra...

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:14.711
Can you put this together in a day?

00:00:16.853 --> 00:00:19.422
Yes, I think it can be done.

00:00:19.422 --> 00:00:20.790
Then, please do that.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.326
I'll be back by then.

00:00:23.326 --> 00:00:25.760
L-I'll come, too...

00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:32.992
I'm counting on you.

00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:40.840
Please wait!

00:00:50.453 --> 00:00:58.194
Nee ima made shiritakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:00:58.194 --> 00:01:04.622
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:16.346
Bokura wa marude
ichimai-chigai no guuzen o sagashiatte

00:01:16.346 --> 00:01:18.515
Meguriatta

00:01:18.515 --> 00:01:26.623
Kimi ga itsuka nomikonda sono kotoba yori

00:01:26.623 --> 00:01:35.532
Zutto iezu ni itekureteta yasashisa o

00:01:35.532 --> 00:01:42.505
Shinjitai to ima omounda

00:01:42.505 --> 00:01:50.246
Nee kono saki wa doko made
mo fuan to tonari-awase

00:01:50.246 --> 00:01:56.653
Nakusu mono ga nakatta
bokutachi wa mou inai

00:01:56.653 --> 00:02:04.360
Nee ima made shiranakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:10.667
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:14.797
Tsumikasanete yuku mono

00:02:20.577 --> 00:02:24.911
"Catastrophe Calls"

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:33.753
I never imagined you'd come to visit me.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.223
It's been so long, Rose.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:42.829
I was so surprised. I never
expected you to be working for the RUC.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.064
Well, a lot happened.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.333
So, when are you coming back?

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:51.137
You can commute from
the apartment, can't you?

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:54.874
When you left, everyone was so worried.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.777
Come by and show everyone
you're doing well.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.179
What do you say?

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:05.785
Sorry, but I have no intention
of returning right now.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:08.310
Excuse me, I have work to do.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.922
Rose!

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.576
Yup, they're there all right.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.578
All over the place.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.080
Are they RUC?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.648
No doubt about it.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.310
Rose told us about them.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:44.057
It's clear that they're
after Integra and Accela.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:47.093
But how did they find this place?

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.729
Sorry, it might've been my fault.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:50.730
You, Roy?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.900
Hey, c'mon, old man,
what's the matter with you?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.103
This is no time to be laying blame.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.839
The question is what do we do next?

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.275
Say, if they're watching us,

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:05.311
does that mean we can't go outside?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.213
Like, not even to school?

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.048
No, not at all.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:13.286
As I said earlier,
they're after Integra and Accela.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:16.989
They could storm this place at any time,
but the reason they haven't

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:21.561
is because they have no solid proof
that the two are here.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.629
Which means now is the time
to make our move.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:24.630
Yeah.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.833
What should we do?

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.235
Act normally.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.237
If we start acting weird and stiff,

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.806
it might actually make us
seem more suspicious.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.109
But you'd better not let your guard down.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.169
They're probably checking
the phones and mail, as well.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.014
The package from Joseph!

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:43.750
Yeah...

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.520
I'll head over to the depot
and have the package held there.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.385
Let's go, Kasha.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:53.693
That leaves Integra and Accela...

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.161
Where's Integra?

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.330
What? Oh, she uh...

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.331
Did she go out?

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.833
W-Well, she...

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:01.968
Solty!

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:04.036
She said she would be back.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.435
Where did she go?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.505
Tell us. Quickly.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:16.282
She asked where Mr. Joseph lived,
so she probably...

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.185
The man who left the message
about the package?

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.253
Yeah.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.245
But why would she go to Joseph's place?

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:36.702
So, why is it that I have to go?

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.070
Beats me.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.306
Oh, please just keep following this road.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:43.342
And why with this guy of all people?

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.812
They must have been
worried about you going alone.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.346
I don't want to hear that from you!

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.015
H-Hey!

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.584
Watch out!

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:55.822
So, you want a hold on deliveries
addressed to Mr. Roy Revant?

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:59.826
Yes. We'll come for any packages later.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:00.593
The address is...

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:05.031
At Fox Avenue and 195th, right?

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:09.302
Someone came early this morning
asking the same thing.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.536
A friend of yours?

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.404
What?

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.206
I told that person, too, but...

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.542
Packages that arrived last night
have already gone out,

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.975
so we can't stop them.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.852
This is it.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:27.620
Ashley Lynx?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.754
Yeah.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:33.359
The man who became the chief investigator
on the RUC murder case?

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.294
Something suspicious about him?

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:38.130
That's what I want you look into.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.000
Isn't he just another RUC elite?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.629
No, that guy's no ordinary elite.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.408
I don't care what it is.

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:52.678
I want information on the guy.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.146
I got you.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:56.415
How can I say no when you ask like that?

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:57.712
I'm counting on you.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:17.003
There is nothing I can do to help.

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:21.667
About all I can do is
go shopping like I always do.

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.315
Excuse me.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:34.887
Yes?

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:38.891
Um, can I help you?

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:42.061
It's been a long time, Dike.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.187
Dike?

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.765
I remember...

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.536
There's no mistake...

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:28.906
This is the Proceed research lab
where they augmented us.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.412
I've been wondering...

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:34.614
What?

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:37.116
You're in love with Rose, aren't you?

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.884
Huh? What?!

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:41.520
How could I be?!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.089
Really?

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:45.324
Since some time ago,
whenever something about Rose came up,

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:47.326
you'd immediately become defensive.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:50.529
So what if I am?!
We're not related by blood!

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.831
See?! I knew it!

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.467
Shut up!

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:57.834
Where could Solty have wandered off to?

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:02.108
She probably just bought too much.

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.541
You think so...

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.743
What?

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:21.293
S-Solty...

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.488
Solty!

00:09:31.671 --> 00:09:34.373
So, now what?

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:37.610
How're we supposed to explain this?!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.146
I don't think we have much
choice but to tell it like it is.

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:42.081
That the cottage was practically destroyed,

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:44.948
and we weren't able
to find Integra, either.

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.630
How is it going?

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.133
Sir, it will take time
to adjust every nerve.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.334
Specifically?

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.234
About 12 hours.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:07.006
Where were you?

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:09.141
I had some business to take care of.

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:12.144
But the problem's been resolved now.

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:13.646
I see.

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:15.681
Rest well.

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.850
When you next awaken,

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.453
our grand endeavor will begin.

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:23.388
Yes, I'll make sure that it does.

00:10:26.692 --> 00:10:29.428
Is brainwashing too difficult, after all?

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.030
We could do it,

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:35.735
but it might disrupt the balance
of her capabilities as a Proceed.

00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:37.202
I see.

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:43.807
Solty!

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:49.849
What happened to her?!

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:52.585
When we found her, she was already...

00:10:52.585 --> 00:10:54.353
Is Solty dead?

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:56.253
Is she? Is she?

00:10:57.289 --> 00:10:59.592
She can't be!

00:10:59.592 --> 00:11:03.796
Isn't there anyone who can fix her?!

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:08.067
Resemble technology
isn't my specialty, so...

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:10.831
If only Yuto were here...

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:18.344
Coming.

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:21.213
Who are you?

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:23.943
Please tell Roy Revant...

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:27.545
...that Joseph is here to see him.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.725
How is she?

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:34.326
This is terrible.

00:11:34.326 --> 00:11:36.962
Ashley probably did this to her.

00:11:36.962 --> 00:11:38.230
What?!

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.132
I don't know if I can repair her,

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:41.997
but I'll take a look.

00:11:45.104 --> 00:11:47.273
Please do that.

00:11:47.273 --> 00:11:50.242
Hey, can we trust that man?

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:52.437
Right now, I don't think we have a choice.

00:11:58.784 --> 00:12:01.353
I'd better hurry and put that together.

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:03.355
Accela.

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:04.824
Integra!

00:12:04.824 --> 00:12:06.158
How did you get inside?!

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:07.393
What about the lookouts?!

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:10.429
I put those guys outside
to sleep for a while.

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:13.499
To sleep? But if you do that...

00:12:13.499 --> 00:12:16.202
This is the package
addressed to Roy Revant.

00:12:16.202 --> 00:12:18.838
It didn't look like
it would be useful to me.

00:12:18.838 --> 00:12:21.006
Give it to him.

00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:22.374
What about what I asked for?

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:24.944
Oh, right. It's almost done.

00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:27.947
All I have to do is
connect the final cord.

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:31.584
I can do that much myself.

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.352
P-Please take...

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:35.287
Please take me with you.

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:37.389
This time, let's work together!

00:12:37.389 --> 00:12:38.324
Accela...

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:41.293
Because... Because...

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:48.434
All right.

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:51.303
Hurry and get ready.

00:12:51.303 --> 00:12:53.168
Right!

00:12:58.344 --> 00:13:00.112
I'm sorry, Accela.

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:00.635
What?

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.123
It's completely fried.

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:14.354
But thanks to this,
the main circuitry was protected.

00:13:16.061 --> 00:13:18.864
I suppose this is
what's called a silver lining.

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.633
This isn't a standard part,

00:13:20.633 --> 00:13:23.193
but it should at least get her running.

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:29.642
Solty...

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:31.243
Are you conscious?

00:13:31.243 --> 00:13:32.645
Solty?

00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:35.681
My name is Dike.

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:37.316
It can't be!

00:13:37.316 --> 00:13:40.513
I came here for the purpose of...

00:13:46.558 --> 00:13:47.793
How'd it go?

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:52.164
I don't have the parts
or tools to repair her here.

00:13:52.164 --> 00:13:53.365
I see.

00:13:53.365 --> 00:13:57.631
Come to think of it,
where's the girl with the short hair?

00:14:20.426 --> 00:14:22.361
What's that?

00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:24.659
That's the direction of the RUC building.

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:28.033
What is it?

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:29.768
A Security Section 7
special command vehicle

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:31.537
just crashed into the 1st floor lobby!

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:32.638
What?!

00:14:32.638 --> 00:14:36.096
We've secured the vehicle, but the
occupant has entered the building.

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:45.150
What are you doing?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:48.320
Moving your own point marker...

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.556
She is my guest.

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:52.387
I will go to greet her.

00:14:55.828 --> 00:14:57.159
Found you!

00:15:00.599 --> 00:15:01.600
Hey.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.158
Get a hold of yourself!

00:15:04.636 --> 00:15:08.273
Hey, that package that
somebody made off with...

00:15:08.273 --> 00:15:10.709
Isn't this it?

00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:12.870
What is it doing here?

00:15:14.913 --> 00:15:16.048
Are you all right?

00:15:16.048 --> 00:15:19.385
L-Integra...

00:15:19.385 --> 00:15:21.620
Where's Integra?!

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.222
Integra?

00:15:23.222 --> 00:15:26.759
I see. Then, that girl is Accela?

00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:29.261
How do you know them?

00:15:29.261 --> 00:15:30.396
What's going on?

00:15:30.396 --> 00:15:31.886
Explain.

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:38.628
Hurry! Hurry!

00:15:40.672 --> 00:15:42.908
They are Proceeds.

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:46.400
I am the one who modified them.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:53.774
Proceeds were created by Blast Fall.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:59.191
The droplets of light that
rained down during Blast Fall

00:15:59.191 --> 00:16:02.361
were none other than the nanomachines

00:16:02.361 --> 00:16:04.830
that form the Aurora Shell.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.765
Nanomachines?

00:16:06.765 --> 00:16:12.604
Very small machines about
6 to 10 millimeter in size.

00:16:12.604 --> 00:16:16.909
When those nanomachines enter
young girls during their growth period,

00:16:16.909 --> 00:16:19.778
they sometimes cause
mutations in their DNA.

00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:22.915
Those girls are Proceeds.

00:16:22.915 --> 00:16:28.253
Every individual Proceed manifests
different special abilities.

00:16:28.253 --> 00:16:30.656
Some gain greater physical abilities.

00:16:30.656 --> 00:16:33.859
Some gain increased visual acuity.

00:16:33.859 --> 00:16:37.129
Some develop enhanced
calculating capabilities.

00:16:37.129 --> 00:16:41.266
But these abilities take
a huge toll on the individual.

00:16:41.266 --> 00:16:43.535
As a result, it becomes
necessary to make adjustments,

00:16:43.535 --> 00:16:45.737
which in effect modify their bodies.

00:16:45.737 --> 00:16:48.307
Why do you know all this?

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:51.777
I became an idle spectator,
because I grew weary of it.

00:16:51.777 --> 00:16:53.679
Answer my question.

00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:59.651
You just said those nanomachines
form the Aurora Shell.

00:16:59.651 --> 00:17:02.313
Is the Aurora Shell man-made?

00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:07.860
Why is there such a thing?

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:12.030
The Aurora Shell was a membrane
used to form a layer of atmosphere

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:15.434
on this planet, which originally
had no air of its own.

00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:17.703
It had no air?

00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:19.771
It was necessary...

00:17:19.771 --> 00:17:22.875
For us humans to live here.

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:26.178
We immigrated here.

00:17:26.178 --> 00:17:27.645
To this planet.

00:17:35.387 --> 00:17:37.514
What is this place?

00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:43.295
It's a ship of hope. My ship of hope.

00:17:43.295 --> 00:17:48.367
With this ship, I will be
free of this despicable planet.

00:17:48.367 --> 00:17:52.504
I won't repeat the mistake
I made 12 years ago.

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:56.008
So you were responsible for Blast Fall!

00:17:56.008 --> 00:17:58.410
It seems you've
done a little homework.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.245
I've been thinking something was amiss.

00:18:00.245 --> 00:18:04.750
Ever since that clock tower incident,
when I rescued Rose on your orders!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:08.487
Proceeds are a new human race
born to this world.

00:18:08.487 --> 00:18:13.325
They are not shackled by a
machine goddess's chains called resemble.

00:18:13.325 --> 00:18:18.697
I did nothing more than use your abilities
to break her spell upon me.

00:18:18.697 --> 00:18:21.366
I don't know what nonsense
you're talking about.

00:18:21.366 --> 00:18:23.602
It doesn't matter.

00:18:23.602 --> 00:18:27.506
You're of no use to me anymore.

00:18:27.506 --> 00:18:29.408
We may have only been co-workers

00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:33.812
who were brought together
purely because we were Proceeds,

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:37.680
but even so, Silvia was a good friend.

00:18:39.418 --> 00:18:45.624
Celica was a handful,
but she was the type you couldn't hate.

00:18:45.624 --> 00:18:49.361
I'm taking revenge for Silvia and Celica!

00:18:49.361 --> 00:18:51.556
Such foolish sentimentality.

00:18:57.336 --> 00:18:59.137
Overclock...

00:18:59.137 --> 00:19:02.941
The capability that enables
momentary high-speed activity.

00:19:02.941 --> 00:19:06.778
However, because it exceeds
the body's physical limits,

00:19:06.778 --> 00:19:09.081
it places a massive strain
on the cerebral nerves.

00:19:09.081 --> 00:19:12.284
And in your case, you can only
use it three times in a row.

00:19:12.284 --> 00:19:14.920
An incredible ability,
but not a very versatile one.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.081
That is your limit.

00:19:25.631 --> 00:19:27.966
Give it up already.

00:19:27.966 --> 00:19:31.069
It must be hard to attack
while destroying brain cells.

00:19:31.069 --> 00:19:32.593
Shut up!

00:19:37.976 --> 00:19:40.579
Now, you have one last time remaining.

00:19:40.579 --> 00:19:44.016
If you stop now, I will
make your death painless.

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:45.677
Don't underestimate me!

00:19:50.489 --> 00:19:52.758
Too bad for you.

00:19:52.758 --> 00:19:55.226
Th-This can't be...

00:19:59.264 --> 00:20:03.035
This is what happens when you
overdo it without maintenance.

00:20:03.035 --> 00:20:06.436
Proceeds are a sad lot.

00:20:10.876 --> 00:20:14.713
This voltage was enough
to lay Dike to rest with one strike.

00:20:14.713 --> 00:20:17.749
It'll be over in an instant.

00:20:17.749 --> 00:20:19.685
Silvia...

00:20:19.685 --> 00:20:21.414
Celica...

00:20:22.788 --> 00:20:25.256
Goodbye, Integra.

00:20:42.741 --> 00:20:46.178
A fourth overclock? What a surprise.

00:20:46.178 --> 00:20:52.250
But my resemble parts aren't
like those imitations out there.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.649
No...

00:20:56.688 --> 00:20:59.057
You're still alive?

00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:01.993
But I doubt you're conscious anymore.

00:21:01.993 --> 00:21:05.588
I'll have you serve as
the bait to lure Accela out.

00:21:32.858 --> 00:21:34.960
You won't get away with this.

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:37.028
You won't get away with this!

00:21:37.028 --> 00:21:39.155
Ashley Lynx!

00:21:52.476 --> 00:21:57.247
Hareta hi no kouen

00:21:57.247 --> 00:22:00.183
Miageta sora ni

00:22:00.183 --> 00:22:08.955
Kiesou ni natta chiisana Little Cloud

00:22:11.461 --> 00:22:16.233
Kaze ni mi o makasete

00:22:16.233 --> 00:22:19.169
Jiyuu ni ikiru

00:22:19.169 --> 00:22:25.574
Sukoshi-zutsu aruku watashi-tachi

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:30.236
Onnaji dane

00:22:31.982 --> 00:22:36.720
Taisetsu na jikan

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:40.557
Deau tabi ni

00:22:40.557 --> 00:22:50.100
Hitori ja nai kono kimochi
yasashisa ni naru

00:22:50.100 --> 00:22:56.707
Dareka o shinjiru yuuki ni kaete

00:22:56.707 --> 00:23:08.483
Kitto kono mama
ano sora no hate ni kieru mae ni

00:23:15.459 --> 00:23:17.894
Where should I start?

00:23:17.894 --> 00:23:19.996
Because I was like that, too.

00:23:19.996 --> 00:23:20.163
Next time, "The Time for Truth".

00:23:20.163 --> 00:23:22.866
Next time, "The Time for Truth".

00:23:22.866 --> 00:23:25.035
Who are you people?
